WEBVTT

00:00:01.920 --> 00:00:14.960
What happened last night with Sven?

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:18.680
I was hoping you'd allow me to introduce you to our Managing Director.

00:00:18.520 --> 00:00:21.360
Kaz, why did you ask me to come here?

00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:22.480
You might knock some sense into her.

00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:26.240
I need a six course, executive luncheon, for less than a tenner a head.

00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:27.640
No problem.

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:29.600
Come on, then!

00:00:28.720 --> 00:00:32.640
Let's see if your bottle's as big as your gob.

00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:37.080
My wife underestimates.

00:00:36.520 --> 00:00:40.120
She has no idea of the things I notice.

00:00:39.400 --> 00:00:43.040
Footage from the day me dad died.

00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:44.680
'Can I see you tomorrow?'

00:01:14.480 --> 00:01:22.640
Mum?

00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:41.200
Hey, guys, who wants some chow?

00:01:48.560 --> 00:01:51.880
Do you actually know what that means?

00:01:59.160 --> 00:02:05.480
Er, hello?

00:02:04.600 --> 00:02:09.080
Fodder?

00:02:08.800 --> 00:02:11.759
Nosebag?

00:02:10.800 --> 00:02:12.200
Nosh?

00:02:11.360 --> 00:02:14.400
What?

00:02:14.160 --> 00:02:18.800
You might wanna choose your words more carefully.

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:22.000
Unless you're actually offering oral sex?

00:02:21.400 --> 00:02:24.080
Hey, if everyone else is up for it!

00:02:23.800 --> 00:02:25.320
Oh, God.

00:02:24.360 --> 00:02:30.440
Oh, I forgot, I'm a parent.

00:02:31.600 --> 00:02:33.240
What's up, Dougie?

00:02:34.160 --> 00:02:37.280
You sitting down?

00:02:36.520 --> 00:02:38.440
Yeah.

00:02:38.280 --> 00:02:42.560
Just had a call from Vinny Haslam.

00:02:41.800 --> 00:02:44.320
That executive dinner?

00:02:43.480 --> 00:02:46.760
Next week, 20 people.

00:02:45.960 --> 00:02:49.360
Pull it off and I get the contract, yeah?

00:02:48.440 --> 00:02:53.440
He wants to bring it forward...to five o'clock today.

00:02:52.800 --> 00:02:54.120
It's a wind-up.

00:02:53.160 --> 00:02:55.120
Piss-take.

00:02:56.040 --> 00:02:57.080
It's like, totally MI, right?

00:02:57.120 --> 00:03:00.760
Mission Impossible.

00:03:02.120 --> 00:03:03.600
Obviously.

00:03:03.320 --> 00:03:05.400
Which is obviously the point.

00:03:04.800 --> 00:03:07.760
Venue unseen?

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:09.760
Up against the clock?

00:03:08.840 --> 00:03:11.440
Can she deliver?

00:03:10.600 --> 00:03:14.240
Nita...

00:03:13.440 --> 00:03:17.160
Guys, how would you like to earn a shed-load of bees?

00:03:16.720 --> 00:03:20.080
Nothing you could offer me would make it worth my while.

00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:22.520
20 squids and I get Magda to muck out your room?

00:03:21.760 --> 00:03:26.240
30 and she does my biology coursework?

00:03:25.320 --> 00:03:26.840
Deal.

00:03:25.880 --> 00:03:27.240
Arlo?

00:03:26.320 --> 00:03:27.480
What can I offer you?

00:03:26.600 --> 00:03:28.640
I'm sure I can think of something.

00:03:28.000 --> 00:03:31.840
You're doing it?

00:03:31.640 --> 00:03:33.080
Creepster!

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:39.880
35, bottle of Baileys AND an Atticus beanie.

00:03:38.920 --> 00:03:41.920
Now we're talking.

00:03:42.320 --> 00:03:44.360
You couldn't afford me.

00:03:43.400 --> 00:03:47.280
Right.

00:03:46.760 --> 00:03:50.240
Who's next?

00:03:49.640 --> 00:03:53.440
Whatever you're selling we don't want it.

00:03:52.560 --> 00:03:57.600
40 quid, crate of Boddies, and two days off in lieu?

00:03:57.200 --> 00:03:58.600
Unbelievable!

00:03:58.320 --> 00:04:03.480
Bit of keg, a few shraps and she thinks she can hijack my day of rest?

00:04:02.520 --> 00:04:05.560
That'll be a yes, then.

00:04:06.480 --> 00:04:11.520
Dennis...can't...sell up.

00:04:11.040 --> 00:04:13.440
Someone needs to talk him out of it.

00:04:12.800 --> 00:04:14.720
Someone?

00:04:13.880 --> 00:04:15.800
Or me?

00:04:15.320 --> 00:04:17.920
Why do you think I'm still here?

00:04:17.079 --> 00:04:21.040
The X Factor?

00:04:20.640 --> 00:04:22.279
What's he on about?

00:04:21.519 --> 00:04:23.720
What's he on about?

00:04:23.080 --> 00:04:28.320
It's the eyesight's gone pluto, Beth not the ears or the nouse.

00:04:27.360 --> 00:04:29.520
Right.

00:04:29.400 --> 00:04:31.760
I'll leave you ladies to it.

00:04:39.920 --> 00:04:44.760
He knows.

00:04:43.960 --> 00:04:45.280
What?

00:04:47.040 --> 00:04:48.280
More than he lets on.

00:04:47.480 --> 00:04:52.920
And he's right about you and Nash.

00:04:54.480 --> 00:04:58.080
You owe him some explanations.

00:04:57.120 --> 00:04:58.800
Do I?

00:04:57.880 --> 00:04:59.000
Mmm.

00:04:58.160 --> 00:05:00.480
Why you left.

00:04:59.880 --> 00:05:02.440
Yeah, like I'm really gonna tell him.

00:05:01.680 --> 00:05:04.920
Not all of it, obviously.

00:05:03.960 --> 00:05:10.520
But isn't it time he knew it wasn't just about him?

00:05:10.520 --> 00:05:13.200
What's she offer you?

00:05:12.360 --> 00:05:17.880
30 quid, a tomato plant and eternal gratitude.

00:05:16.920 --> 00:05:18.720
Hiya.

00:05:18.080 --> 00:05:19.640
Hiya.

00:05:18.800 --> 00:05:21.280
Notice she didn't ask you.

00:05:20.320 --> 00:05:21.680
I couldn't, anyway.

00:05:20.800 --> 00:05:22.520
I'm on a mission, remember?

00:05:21.680 --> 00:05:22.960
Oh, yeah.

00:05:22.040 --> 00:05:23.240
Just the one?

00:06:00.480 --> 00:06:01.560
Oh!

00:06:00.960 --> 00:06:04.120
I thought you'd be someone else.

00:06:03.360 --> 00:06:04.880
Who?

00:06:04.360 --> 00:06:07.400
A potential buyer, actually.

00:06:06.480 --> 00:06:11.280
Oh, really.

00:06:15.400 --> 00:06:19.600
Why d'you think I've never had a boyfriend?

00:06:18.720 --> 00:06:20.560
Can't imagine.

00:06:19.960 --> 00:06:21.760
Do you think it's weird?

00:06:21.000 --> 00:06:23.200
Er, no.

00:06:22.640 --> 00:06:23.720
Not in your case.

00:06:22.840 --> 00:06:28.520
I suppose I've never been that fussed about lads.

00:06:27.560 --> 00:06:28.600
Mmm.

00:06:27.840 --> 00:06:32.160
Could never really see myself getting involved.

00:06:31.280 --> 00:06:35.720
But now I think, yeah, why not?

00:06:34.840 --> 00:06:36.320
BETH SIGHS Yeah...

00:06:35.400 --> 00:06:37.840
If it was the right person.

00:06:37.280 --> 00:06:39.320
He don't exist, Al.

00:06:38.360 --> 00:06:40.240
I think he might.

00:06:39.600 --> 00:06:42.720
Oh, dream on.

00:06:41.880 --> 00:06:45.040
Oh, I do.

00:06:44.080 --> 00:06:45.440
All the time.

00:06:44.480 --> 00:06:45.680
Mmm.

00:06:44.800 --> 00:06:47.320
All kinds of dreams.

00:06:46.480 --> 00:06:47.600
Mmm.

00:06:47.000 --> 00:06:49.360
Yeah, you don't say!

00:06:48.400 --> 00:06:51.440
Dreams are important.

00:06:50.520 --> 00:06:54.640
Bryce says we should always pay attention to dreams.

00:06:53.880 --> 00:06:57.560
The one this morning, well, I think it was important.

00:06:56.640 --> 00:07:00.680
Well, Bryce says everything's important.

00:06:59.840 --> 00:07:05.240
He says we should always look for the hidden agenda.

00:07:04.480 --> 00:07:11.640
So in the dream, it's like I was her, I was Mum, collecting the letter I wrote, asking her to come home.

00:07:10.680 --> 00:07:11.840
Where?

00:07:11.000 --> 00:07:14.080
Marrakech, I suppose.

00:07:13.240 --> 00:07:16.200
That's where I sent it, that post restauranty place Phil gave me.

00:07:15.440 --> 00:07:17.840
I think I should tell Bryce.

00:07:17.160 --> 00:07:18.640
Mmm.

00:07:18.040 --> 00:07:23.640
He said to let him know if there's any developments, any progress with me.

00:07:23.080 --> 00:07:24.720
How likely is that?

00:07:23.960 --> 00:07:25.520
..

00:07:24.600 --> 00:07:25.720
Let me in, for Christ's sake!

00:07:24.840 --> 00:07:27.120
She's pecking me head in.

00:07:26.520 --> 00:07:29.240
I were just telling her about this dream I had.

00:07:28.560 --> 00:07:36.760
Finally, 6.45, clear course six, and serve coffee, liqueurs and petit fours.

00:07:35.920 --> 00:07:37.920
Any questions?

00:07:37.200 --> 00:07:39.040
When did you first realise you'd lost the plot?

00:07:38.520 --> 00:07:39.680
Next?

00:07:38.760 --> 00:07:40.440
When do the others get here?

00:07:39.640 --> 00:07:41.120
Which?

00:07:40.520 --> 00:07:46.720
The ten extra pair of hands we'll need if we've any chance of delivering what you just described.

00:07:45.920 --> 00:07:48.200
That's the difference between us, Beth.

00:07:47.960 --> 00:07:51.680
You see a problem, I see a challenge.

00:07:50.720 --> 00:07:54.720
No, the difference is I have a conscience, you take the piss.

00:07:53.760 --> 00:07:57.920
You expect people to do you a favour on shit wages.

00:07:57.120 --> 00:07:58.320
Me, I wouldn't even ask.

00:07:57.720 --> 00:08:02.360
Which is why I have a turnover of half a million a year, and you're still frying bacon.

00:08:02.040 --> 00:08:04.440
.. OK, guys, pinnies on.

00:08:03.520 --> 00:08:04.880
Wow!

00:08:03.960 --> 00:08:06.720
She's hard-core, your mum.

00:08:06.080 --> 00:08:08.400
Don't even think about being impressed.

00:08:10.120 --> 00:08:14.440
Building bridges.

00:08:14.240 --> 00:08:16.080
Making amends.

00:08:15.560 --> 00:08:19.800
All so easy, 20 years too late.

00:08:18.920 --> 00:08:22.880
I just thought if we could go out for a drink, just you and me.

00:08:22.120 --> 00:08:23.960
I don't do out.

00:08:23.000 --> 00:08:25.360
Since when?

00:08:24.560 --> 00:08:29.680
Since you nobbed off, and I stayed in to mind Head the Ball.

00:08:29.000 --> 00:08:32.840
Dennis, I know what that must've been like.

00:08:32.080 --> 00:08:33.440
Do you?

00:08:32.600 --> 00:08:34.240
Every day?

00:08:33.679 --> 00:08:38.600
Watching him shrivel, pining for the Marrakech trollop.

00:08:37.720 --> 00:08:44.080
Letters that never arrived, kids that never visited, grandkids he's never even seen!

00:08:43.200 --> 00:08:44.480
He deserved better.

00:08:44.159 --> 00:08:45.440
OK?

00:08:44.520 --> 00:08:47.160
YOU deserved better.

00:08:46.440 --> 00:08:49.800
Like you give a shit.

00:08:49.080 --> 00:08:50.880
I do, actually.

00:08:50.160 --> 00:08:54.840
I wasn't happy, leaving you to deal with him, but at the time it seemed...

00:08:54.120 --> 00:08:58.240
What did it seem?

00:08:58.080 --> 00:08:59.960
Like the only option.

00:09:05.560 --> 00:09:08.480
Do you ever hear from her?

00:09:08.840 --> 00:09:10.360
Do you know what?

00:09:10.640 --> 00:09:12.760
No.

00:09:13.040 --> 00:09:17.120
Apparently it's only you she keeps in touch with.

00:09:16.520 --> 00:09:19.360
Just the odd postcard.

00:09:19.560 --> 00:09:22.880
Well, aren't you the favoured one?

00:09:23.320 --> 00:09:29.400
As far as we were concerned, she might as well not exist.

00:09:28.440 --> 00:09:32.040
Valium.

00:09:31.160 --> 00:09:32.640
You need this?

00:09:33.800 --> 00:09:35.000
No, not remotely!

00:09:34.120 --> 00:09:38.800
20 years caring for Alco-Pop.

00:09:38.040 --> 00:09:47.320
Sat in here so long, I can't even step out my own front door for more than half an hour, and even then I need a gang of bow-wows as armed escort.

00:09:46.400 --> 00:09:48.760
No, course I don't need it!

00:09:52.560 --> 00:10:01.880
Anyhow, since you're here, I expect you'd like to hear what some of the prospective buyers have talked about doing to the place.

00:10:14.280 --> 00:10:20.440
Diced, guys, not bludgeoned to a pulp.

00:10:19.560 --> 00:10:27.320
How do you fancy two tickets for Michael Buble and a bottle of Asti?

00:10:26.440 --> 00:10:29.800
One guy was talking about knocking through the whole ground floor, doing the open-plan thing.

00:10:29.440 --> 00:10:34.320
And then pushing down into the cellars and making a new basement flat.

00:10:33.600 --> 00:10:37.320
Wow.

00:10:36.480 --> 00:10:38.480
Who'd want to live down here?

00:10:37.560 --> 00:10:40.480
It's so poky and dark.

00:10:39.800 --> 00:10:43.160
Well, at the moment, yeah.

00:10:42.200 --> 00:10:45.320
They'd need to excavate, obviously.

00:10:44.440 --> 00:10:46.640
What?

00:10:46.480 --> 00:10:49.560
You know, lower the floor.

00:10:49.360 --> 00:10:50.520
They'd need more height.

00:10:49.880 --> 00:10:51.400
SHE SIGHS Dennis.

00:10:50.600 --> 00:10:52.080
Yeah?

00:10:51.120 --> 00:10:53.480
Are you sure about this?

00:10:52.640 --> 00:10:55.680
It's been your home for 40 years.

00:10:54.880 --> 00:10:59.160
You'd be mad to sell if you're so attached.

00:10:58.400 --> 00:11:00.080
I'm not.

00:10:59.320 --> 00:11:02.200
Why would I be?

00:11:01.320 --> 00:11:05.440
This place reminds me of everything I detest.

00:11:04.520 --> 00:11:08.840
Secrets, dishonesty, denial.

00:11:08.320 --> 00:11:10.520
Denial?

00:11:11.920 --> 00:11:14.080
Er, these, for instance.

00:11:13.480 --> 00:11:14.680
This.

00:11:13.760 --> 00:11:18.880
You don't think it's weird that not one person has asked me why.

00:11:18.000 --> 00:11:19.120
Well, maybe...

00:11:18.320 --> 00:11:20.600
Not one person!

00:11:19.800 --> 00:11:21.400
OK, then.

00:11:20.440 --> 00:11:22.480
Why?

00:11:24.040 --> 00:11:28.760
Our dear departed mother.

00:11:27.880 --> 00:11:31.960
Metaphorically speaking.

00:11:32.480 --> 00:11:44.040
After she bailed out, me and Dad were going through some of her stuff - scent, nail varnish, make-up.

00:11:44.160 --> 00:11:45.520
I put some on.

00:11:44.600 --> 00:11:48.320
Make him laugh, I thought.

00:11:47.440 --> 00:11:48.640
He didn't laugh.

00:11:47.680 --> 00:11:51.000
He freaked out.

00:11:50.200 --> 00:11:52.800
Well, that was it.

00:11:52.280 --> 00:11:58.480
I kept going back to it and going back and when it was used up I bought some more.

00:11:58.120 --> 00:11:59.680
But Dad, he was such a bigot.

00:11:58.800 --> 00:12:01.200
Cope?

00:12:00.320 --> 00:12:01.680
He didn't.

00:12:00.760 --> 00:12:03.920
He went feral every time.

00:12:03.360 --> 00:12:07.400
Why do you think I did it?

00:12:06.840 --> 00:12:12.000
To wind him up.

00:12:12.560 --> 00:12:14.560
So it was just...?

00:12:14.600 --> 00:12:18.480
So you're not actually...?

00:12:17.600 --> 00:12:19.440
Tranny Two Shoes?

00:12:18.880 --> 00:12:20.080
Might be.

00:12:19.160 --> 00:12:21.000
Might not.

00:12:20.400 --> 00:12:22.840
Who wants to know?

00:12:22.080 --> 00:12:24.000
Answer?

00:12:23.160 --> 00:12:25.240
No-one.

00:12:24.760 --> 00:12:28.800
No-one dares.

00:12:29.120 --> 00:12:32.720
"Deviant in the room, let's pretend it's not happening."

00:12:32.120 --> 00:12:33.840
Well, it is happening.

00:12:33.120 --> 00:12:38.200
It's all happening, Phil, and you'd better wake up to the idea.

00:12:37.600 --> 00:12:42.240
Including the fact that I am most definitely selling up.

00:12:44.440 --> 00:12:50.280
So I suggest you go away and decide what you wanna do next.

00:12:57.680 --> 00:13:00.000
Can you believe this?

00:12:59.320 --> 00:13:04.720
House full of people who'd sooner be out getting wankered or still in bed?

00:13:04.000 --> 00:13:08.160
Instead of which they're all here, doing what she wants.

00:13:07.560 --> 00:13:10.640
How do they fall for it every time?

00:13:09.680 --> 00:13:11.880
Cos she knows just how to reel them in.

00:13:11.160 --> 00:13:13.400
She gives it the face.

00:13:12.520 --> 00:13:16.360
The big eyes, soft voice, the guilt trip, the bribe.

00:13:16.400 --> 00:13:17.960
HORN TOOTS Not to mention the 'string 'em along in the hope of a shag'.

00:13:22.400 --> 00:13:23.640
(Hiya. )

00:13:27.640 --> 00:13:32.520
'So guess where I am.'

00:13:33.360 --> 00:13:35.320
Inside or out?

00:13:36.960 --> 00:13:38.440
Out.

00:13:39.160 --> 00:13:42.600
The tree.

00:13:41.640 --> 00:13:43.400
How's the artwork?

00:13:43.520 --> 00:13:50.040
Well, I'm guessing your carpentry skills are a bit more... refined these days.

00:13:52.520 --> 00:13:55.000
What a loser!

00:13:54.240 --> 00:13:56.400
So when can I see you?

00:13:55.520 --> 00:13:57.640
Soon as.

00:13:56.920 --> 00:13:58.480
Where?

00:13:57.880 --> 00:14:01.840
West Dene.

00:14:04.960 --> 00:14:07.400
You're kidding!

00:14:06.640 --> 00:14:10.480
KNOCK ON DOOR Anybody home?

00:14:09.920 --> 00:14:12.240
Coming, Dougie.

00:14:11.680 --> 00:14:14.680
Look, you know where to look.

00:14:13.840 --> 00:14:15.960
I've gotta go.

00:14:15.040 --> 00:14:16.280
Just get there.

00:14:15.320 --> 00:14:17.680
Wait for me.

00:14:22.480 --> 00:14:24.640
Dougie, don't look so worried!

00:14:24.280 --> 00:14:27.280
I just hope you know what you're taking on.

00:14:26.600 --> 00:14:30.560
Thought I'd drop by, check it's all under control.

00:14:30.000 --> 00:14:32.040
You know Nita.

00:14:31.160 --> 00:14:34.280
Military precision in all things.

00:14:34.040 --> 00:14:37.760
Right, I'm short of waiters.

00:14:36.800 --> 00:14:38.960
Do you fancy pitching in?

00:14:38.280 --> 00:14:39.840
Er...

00:14:39.000 --> 00:14:40.240
I would, but I'm one of the guests.

00:14:39.560 --> 00:14:44.800
Vinny's asked me to escort his niece.

00:14:46.120 --> 00:14:47.600
And this niece is how old?

00:14:46.720 --> 00:14:49.480
About 22.

00:14:50.360 --> 00:14:56.240
But can I just say I think you should be turning your thoughts to the venue.

00:14:55.440 --> 00:14:58.520
He's not thinking of pairing you off with her?

00:14:57.840 --> 00:15:01.040
I'm not sure what exactly you're expecting.

00:15:00.360 --> 00:15:03.880
We both know you'd be better off with someone more mature.

00:15:03.520 --> 00:15:06.960
I think it might present something of a challenge.

00:15:06.080 --> 00:15:11.240
Not a looker, and not a smart-arse - you don't want her giving you the run-around.

00:15:10.320 --> 00:15:13.640
What sort of a challenge?

00:15:12.760 --> 00:15:17.640
Let's just say it's lucky that your husband's a master carpenter.

00:15:22.280 --> 00:15:24.280
I need a favour.

00:15:23.480 --> 00:15:24.520
Please?

00:15:23.600 --> 00:15:26.320
Pretty please?

00:15:34.080 --> 00:15:37.800
Well, far be it from me to state the obvious.

00:15:37.280 --> 00:15:42.680
I know, but it's what Haslam wants.

00:15:41.840 --> 00:15:44.800
It's his new baby, he wants to show it off.

00:15:44.000 --> 00:15:47.280
I did warn Nita it wouldn't be straightforward.

00:15:46.360 --> 00:15:52.880
Can you build me a frame so we can light the table from above?

00:15:51.920 --> 00:15:54.680
And Dougie, you've OK'd it so we can use the on-site kitchen?

00:15:53.720 --> 00:15:54.880
Cool.

00:15:54.000 --> 00:16:00.200
So we'll need the chairs and the fold-up table we used for the staff Christmas dinner.

00:15:59.440 --> 00:16:03.240
Plus our table linen, cutlery, glassware.

00:16:02.440 --> 00:16:06.160
Nita, I really don't think you need to go this far.

00:16:05.200 --> 00:16:06.600
Oh, you don't?

00:16:05.760 --> 00:16:09.840
So I needn't push the boat out and lay on a really spectacular show?

00:16:09.000 --> 00:16:15.400
I shouldn't aim to have the contract in the bag by the end of the meal?

00:16:14.640 --> 00:16:16.800
Yes, but Nita, in two hours?

00:16:19.360 --> 00:16:21.360
I'll get my tools.

00:16:24.080 --> 00:16:32.120
Did I tell you the weird thing that happened yesterday in my session with Bryce?

00:16:31.200 --> 00:16:35.360
Please tell me he hypnotised himself into a coma?

00:16:34.600 --> 00:16:37.280
Don't encourage her.

00:16:36.400 --> 00:16:38.400
You'll never hear the last of it.

00:16:37.640 --> 00:16:40.920
Aren't you glad she's getting some help?

00:16:39.960 --> 00:16:41.520
No!

00:16:40.680 --> 00:16:44.280
I prefer her screwed up and quiet.

00:16:44.080 --> 00:16:47.600
SHE MOUTHS Do you fancy him?

00:16:47.120 --> 00:16:48.320
No.

00:16:47.640 --> 00:16:49.840
Think about him all the time?

00:16:48.880 --> 00:16:50.680
Imagine him tongue-wrestling you?

00:16:50.400 --> 00:16:51.840
No!

00:16:51.320 --> 00:16:53.600
What you doing?

00:16:52.760 --> 00:16:54.480
Phoning him.

00:16:53.760 --> 00:16:55.760
Lola!

00:16:54.960 --> 00:16:57.920
Well, find out what his game is, what his intentions are.

00:16:57.120 --> 00:16:58.800
No, don't!

00:16:57.880 --> 00:16:59.640
Give me the phone.

00:16:58.880 --> 00:17:00.560
Oh, it's ringing!

00:17:06.440 --> 00:17:10.200
'Bryce Waghorn?'

00:17:09.400 --> 00:17:10.960
Yes.

00:17:10.079 --> 00:17:12.520
I'm calling about Alice Tyler.

00:17:12.040 --> 00:17:13.359
Yeah?

00:17:12.400 --> 00:17:14.599
What about her?

00:17:13.800 --> 00:17:18.640
Well, I understand you've been subjecting her to some rather unusual practices.

00:17:17.800 --> 00:17:20.400
What do you mean?

00:17:19.760 --> 00:17:22.000
Well, some very unorthodox methods.

00:17:21.359 --> 00:17:23.240
Who is this?

00:17:22.480 --> 00:17:24.920
Look, I don't know what she's been telling you, but...

00:17:24.680 --> 00:17:28.000
Well, whatever you've done, it's worked.

00:17:27.040 --> 00:17:29.280
Cos, er, she's got the hots for you.

00:17:28.440 --> 00:17:29.600
Don't!

00:17:28.640 --> 00:17:31.360
Give me the phone.

00:17:30.400 --> 00:17:31.560
Ah, sweet!

00:17:30.680 --> 00:17:34.400
She's blushing!

00:17:34.120 --> 00:17:38.360
God, I am so sorry.

00:17:37.480 --> 00:17:40.800
That was my niece, just ignore her.

00:17:40.080 --> 00:17:41.800
I have never at any point...

00:17:41.720 --> 00:17:45.200
Alice, it's OK.

00:17:44.400 --> 00:17:49.320
What she's saying is not exactly news to me.

00:17:48.400 --> 00:17:50.880
What d'you mean?

00:17:49.920 --> 00:17:53.080
It's a well-known phenomenon.

00:17:52.120 --> 00:17:56.160
Clients having strong feelings for their therapists.

00:17:55.200 --> 00:17:57.960
It's called transference.

00:17:57.520 --> 00:17:58.840
No, but...

00:17:58.320 --> 00:18:02.200
It's by no means a bad thing if it facilitates the process.

00:18:01.480 --> 00:18:04.320
It engenders a greater sense of trust.

00:18:03.440 --> 00:18:07.200
So...lots of people feel like this?

00:18:06.280 --> 00:18:07.720
I'm...

00:18:06.960 --> 00:18:09.040
I'm not sort of weird?

00:18:08.240 --> 00:18:10.760
No, no, not at all.

00:18:10.280 --> 00:18:12.560
Refreshingly normal.

00:18:12.880 --> 00:18:19.560
In fact, so normal, I doubt you'll be needing to see me much longer.

00:18:18.600 --> 00:18:21.520
But I want to.

00:18:20.680 --> 00:18:21.840
I need to.

00:18:20.920 --> 00:18:25.280
You're the only person who doesn't take the piss.

00:18:24.520 --> 00:18:26.920
Well, you can.

00:18:26.400 --> 00:18:28.040
When?

00:18:27.200 --> 00:18:29.080
Soon?

00:18:28.240 --> 00:18:34.800
I've got a pretty full schedule but I might just be able to carve out an hour this afternoon.

00:18:34.160 --> 00:18:37.760
SHE SIGHS I can't, I'm working.

00:18:36.960 --> 00:18:39.280
Best leave it, then.

00:18:38.360 --> 00:18:39.880
No!

00:18:39.080 --> 00:18:42.000
No, I'll see what I can manage.

00:18:41.120 --> 00:18:42.600
I'll get a taxi or something.

00:18:41.640 --> 00:18:43.240
I've gotta go.

00:18:49.520 --> 00:18:52.960
OK, I've thought.

00:18:52.400 --> 00:18:56.520
I'd like to make an offer on the place myself.

00:18:58.320 --> 00:19:01.560
Listen up!

00:19:00.640 --> 00:19:06.440
Whatever stage we're at, I want you to finish off, pack up and move across to the venue.

00:19:05.560 --> 00:19:11.840
We've got less than two hours to complete food prep, plate up, and create a dining room out of a building site.

00:19:11.000 --> 00:19:12.120
Peasy.

00:19:11.240 --> 00:19:15.040
You'll need your smart clothes, aprons...

00:19:14.120 --> 00:19:17.200
Sense of humour.

00:19:16.240 --> 00:19:17.560
And the ability to clamp your beak when you feel a moan coming on.

00:19:16.680 --> 00:19:21.040
And I still need three more waiters, so any sensible suggestions, let me know.

00:19:20.080 --> 00:19:21.400
OK, let's move.

00:19:32.760 --> 00:19:39.800
Nice way to spend a Sunday.

00:19:39.720 --> 00:19:42.600
Girls, come on, it's for us, not just me.

00:19:41.640 --> 00:19:44.400
We deliver the goods, we get the contract.

00:19:43.560 --> 00:19:46.480
We get the contract, we're all in the mint.

00:19:45.800 --> 00:19:48.640
Except some of us are more minted than others.

00:20:02.640 --> 00:20:05.920
OK, guys, food in here.

00:20:05.320 --> 00:20:10.760
Cutlery, crockery, glassware, follow me.

00:20:21.480 --> 00:20:25.440
Hello?

00:20:24.840 --> 00:20:28.640
Hero worship?

00:20:27.720 --> 00:20:30.880
Isn't this guy just a total star?

00:20:30.120 --> 00:20:33.320
How can I ever repay you?

00:20:32.800 --> 00:20:39.720
By never again reneging on our agreement to keep our businesses totally separate.

00:20:42.560 --> 00:20:48.720
Dougie, can you organise the seating?

00:20:47.920 --> 00:20:51.240
Ethan, Lola, give him a hand.

00:20:50.840 --> 00:20:53.200
Arlo, come with me.

00:20:55.760 --> 00:20:59.240
You're well fit, you know that?

00:20:58.280 --> 00:21:02.920
Let's just pretend you didn't say that and I didn't hear it.

00:21:02.160 --> 00:21:06.680
Say the word and I'll give Lola the push.

00:21:06.080 --> 00:21:08.280
Why would you do that?

00:21:07.440 --> 00:21:08.920
I think we have a future.

00:21:08.400 --> 00:21:09.720
You and me.

00:21:08.800 --> 00:21:12.360
Sweetheart, I think we need to talk.

00:21:11.400 --> 00:21:13.440
Dennis, now is not a good moment.

00:21:13.680 --> 00:21:16.680
Well, that's cool, cos it's not great news.

00:21:16.520 --> 00:21:19.960
I've had another offer for the house.

00:21:19.280 --> 00:21:20.520
How?

00:21:19.560 --> 00:21:21.720
Surely no-one else knows you're selling?

00:21:20.960 --> 00:21:23.640
Who's it from?

00:21:23.000 --> 00:21:27.680
Oh, you surely wouldn't want me breaking client confidentiality by giving you a name?

00:21:27.880 --> 00:21:31.760
'Course, you could always up your bid.

00:21:30.880 --> 00:21:33.760
'I know you wouldn't want me being short-changed.'

00:21:32.840 --> 00:21:37.880
Specially if we've both misread the market.

00:21:37.760 --> 00:21:40.960
Dennis, can I get back to you?

00:21:40.080 --> 00:21:43.880
Obviously I want to make sure you're getting a fair price.

00:21:43.000 --> 00:21:44.800
It's just now's not a good time.

00:21:43.880 --> 00:21:45.080
Oh!

00:21:56.440 --> 00:22:02.040
Did I mention how much interest there's been?

00:22:01.280 --> 00:22:04.080
Oh, I don't mean recently.

00:22:03.400 --> 00:22:05.720
Since before Dad died.

00:22:05.240 --> 00:22:07.560
You didn't, no.

00:22:07.320 --> 00:22:10.040
Whole rake of enquiries.

00:22:09.480 --> 00:22:10.800
Well, I say "enquiries".

00:22:10.000 --> 00:22:14.280
At first we thought it was pranksters.

00:22:13.560 --> 00:22:18.480
Threats, incentives, you name it, they just kept coming.

00:22:17.600 --> 00:22:22.560
In fact, we began to wonder if there wasn't a bigger picture.

00:22:22.000 --> 00:22:24.920
That's when we started recording the calls.

00:22:24.120 --> 00:22:26.080
Really?

00:22:25.200 --> 00:22:26.760
And?

00:22:26.120 --> 00:22:27.440
Interesting.

00:22:26.480 --> 00:22:29.200
Could I listen?

00:22:28.440 --> 00:22:30.360
Why not?

00:22:43.320 --> 00:22:51.040
WOMAN ON 'You do realise this area's going to be bulldozed to make way for a new motorway?

00:22:50.640 --> 00:22:53.920
'If I were you I'd sell up now, while you can still get a decent price.'

00:22:52.960 --> 00:22:54.520
Any more?

00:22:54.440 --> 00:22:56.520
Oh, sure, if you're interested.

00:22:57.360 --> 00:23:01.960
'Listen, pal, I can only protect you for so long.

00:23:01.000 --> 00:23:06.160
'My superior's not a patient man, and when he wants something...'

00:23:05.760 --> 00:23:08.120
That's a bit scary.

00:23:08.640 --> 00:23:09.880
Any more?

00:23:09.080 --> 00:23:17.600
'Hello, I'm doing a survey for the Eccles and Patricroft Bugle.

00:23:16.720 --> 00:23:22.800
I'm wondering what you, as a resident of Elgin Park, think of the recent crime wave in your area?

00:23:21.920 --> 00:23:23.080
'You what?

00:23:22.120 --> 00:23:27.760
Can you say you feel safe in your home these days with feral gangs roaming the streets?'

00:23:27.240 --> 00:23:31.920
That's the form these days, is it?

00:23:31.120 --> 00:23:36.960
You see a place you like, you put the bite on the owners?

00:23:36.880 --> 00:23:38.200
No, it's really not.

00:23:37.440 --> 00:23:39.400
It's weird, though.

00:23:38.440 --> 00:23:42.840
Sudden mad spurt of interest, all these people desperate to buy.

00:23:44.200 --> 00:23:45.880
Yeah.

00:23:45.040 --> 00:23:48.000
Unless it's the same person.

00:23:48.320 --> 00:23:51.920
Oh, c'mon!

00:23:51.280 --> 00:23:55.880
Who would seriously sink so low?

00:24:03.680 --> 00:24:05.880
Don't let me keep you!

00:24:04.920 --> 00:24:06.160
I won't.

00:24:06.920 --> 00:24:10.600
You don't seem too curious about these calls.

00:24:09.840 --> 00:24:12.800
It's water under the bridge.

00:24:11.920 --> 00:24:18.320
No, but what's weird, that last one, the thing about feral gangs...

00:24:17.800 --> 00:24:18.920
Yeah?

00:24:18.160 --> 00:24:22.120
Well, the night Dad died, there was a gang, wasn't there?

00:24:21.440 --> 00:24:23.320
Yeah, but...

00:24:22.480 --> 00:24:24.880
A gang, Dennis.

00:24:23.960 --> 00:24:26.560
Was it coincidence?

00:24:25.680 --> 00:24:27.760
Well, what else would it be?

00:24:26.800 --> 00:24:30.200
Had you ever seen them before?

00:24:29.360 --> 00:24:30.480
No.

00:24:29.520 --> 00:24:31.920
Would you recognise them again?

00:24:31.000 --> 00:24:32.520
No.

00:24:31.960 --> 00:24:34.200
Not that I haven't tried.

00:24:33.400 --> 00:24:38.360
Played back the tape enough times.

00:24:37.480 --> 00:24:38.640
Tape?

00:24:37.800 --> 00:24:43.800
Security cam footage from the night it happened.

00:24:42.840 --> 00:24:44.520
You still have it?

00:24:43.600 --> 00:24:45.240
Somewhere.

00:24:44.440 --> 00:24:46.920
Could I see it?

00:25:03.920 --> 00:25:07.360
Could be anyone.

00:25:10.120 --> 00:25:11.480
This is it.

00:25:14.960 --> 00:25:18.200
This is what did it for Dad.

00:25:17.640 --> 00:25:21.560
This is what brought on his heart attack.

00:25:27.880 --> 00:25:35.800
But as you can see, it's all so blurred, totally unrecognisable.

00:25:37.960 --> 00:25:44.640
So... there's not much point in pursuing it any further.

00:25:43.920 --> 00:25:45.920
Is there?

00:25:45.280 --> 00:25:47.160
I don't know.

00:25:46.400 --> 00:25:50.440
I need to think.

00:25:49.760 --> 00:25:54.040
You think there might be something we should follow up?

00:25:53.440 --> 00:25:55.720
I don't know.

00:25:54.920 --> 00:25:57.440
I need to think.

00:26:03.480 --> 00:26:06.840
These girls.

00:26:05.880 --> 00:26:09.080
They think they know it all.

00:26:08.440 --> 00:26:10.440
But they haven't got a clue.

00:26:19.160 --> 00:26:25.160
How come you never told me you were outside Dad's house the night he died?

00:26:24.320 --> 00:26:26.840
Chill, guys.

00:26:25.960 --> 00:26:29.240
Take a breath.

00:26:30.320 --> 00:26:31.440
Can't talk.

00:26:30.600 --> 00:26:33.320
It's Armageddon Central here.

00:26:32.360 --> 00:26:35.440
I'll call you later.

00:26:34.560 --> 00:26:37.040
Shit.

00:26:43.120 --> 00:26:47.360
'Hi, it's Beth, you know what to do.'

00:26:46.640 --> 00:26:48.800
Beth, call me back.

00:26:47.920 --> 00:26:49.480
Now!

00:26:49.640 --> 00:26:51.960
45 minutes.

00:26:51.360 --> 00:26:54.840
Beth, Alice, start laying out the appetisers.

00:26:53.880 --> 00:26:58.320
Lois, you're in charge of salads.

00:26:57.360 --> 00:26:58.560
Nancy, you're garnishings.

00:26:57.640 --> 00:27:00.200
Ethan, you're washing up.

00:26:59.480 --> 00:27:01.480
Right.

00:27:00.520 --> 00:27:03.720
Did anyone come up with any waiters?

00:27:07.040 --> 00:27:08.200
Er...

00:27:07.240 --> 00:27:10.760
20 squids and a case of Stella apiece?

00:27:10.400 --> 00:27:12.840
You are joking!

00:27:11.880 --> 00:27:16.200
I said desperate, not a death wish!

00:27:15.440 --> 00:27:16.720
I'm silver-service trained.

00:27:15.880 --> 00:27:17.040
Used to wait on at Talk Of The North.

00:27:16.560 --> 00:27:18.760
We'll point him in the right direction!

00:27:17.840 --> 00:27:19.720
Coolio!

00:27:20.160 --> 00:27:23.840
OK!

00:27:22.920 --> 00:27:25.480
Come in, grab a pinny.

00:27:24.680 --> 00:27:28.560
Anyone ever served wine?

00:27:28.920 --> 00:27:30.600
Down his neck at the rate of four kegs a night!

00:27:29.760 --> 00:27:34.240
OK, so these are your roles for the rest of the afternoon.

00:27:34.240 --> 00:27:38.760
Please listen, it gets boring when I have to repeat myself.

00:27:40.400 --> 00:27:43.320
Right, switches.

00:27:42.360 --> 00:27:48.440
These are your lights, this is your audio here.

00:27:47.760 --> 00:27:49.400
You're going?

00:27:48.720 --> 00:27:50.800
Yeah.

00:27:50.040 --> 00:27:52.480
Sure you won't need it.

00:27:52.200 --> 00:27:57.600
You know, it's time's like this a girl really needs someone to hold her hand.

00:27:56.800 --> 00:28:00.360
Nita, I have never met anyone less in need of hand-holding.

00:27:59.440 --> 00:28:01.720
Whereas me, I'm in need of a beer.

00:28:01.200 --> 00:28:02.800
You could have one here.

00:28:01.840 --> 00:28:03.560
I really don't wanna be here.

00:28:02.600 --> 00:28:06.160
It's my Sunday.

00:28:05.280 --> 00:28:07.360
Where are you going?

00:28:06.640 --> 00:28:08.800
What's with the inquisition?

00:28:08.040 --> 00:28:10.320
I know where you're going.

00:28:09.840 --> 00:28:13.560
I can absolutely guarantee you don't.

00:28:12.880 --> 00:28:14.560
Nash, wait.

00:28:13.640 --> 00:28:14.760
Nita?

00:28:13.800 --> 00:28:15.400
Don't go.

00:28:15.440 --> 00:28:18.120
I think you're wanted.

00:28:18.240 --> 00:28:21.320
I've just had a call from Sven.

00:28:20.360 --> 00:28:22.760
They're on their way.

00:28:21.840 --> 00:28:25.320
But they're half an hour early!

00:28:24.760 --> 00:28:26.880
Of course they are!

00:28:26.240 --> 00:28:28.560
That's the point, right?

00:28:27.600 --> 00:28:30.560
OK.

00:28:36.280 --> 00:28:41.240
We can do this.

00:29:09.600 --> 00:29:17.400
Is that your court appearance outfit?

00:29:25.960 --> 00:29:32.200
I can manage!

00:29:35.200 --> 00:29:41.640
Oh, yeah, since when?

00:29:42.200 --> 00:29:45.360
I'm not getting shown up by you looking like a toerag!

00:30:00.360 --> 00:30:03.200
'Eagle Cars.'

00:30:02.320 --> 00:30:05.480
Hello?

00:30:07.040 --> 00:30:12.000
'Yes, love.'

00:30:17.560 --> 00:30:20.000
Can I book a cab, please?

00:30:49.400 --> 00:31:06.200
You kept our flat.

00:31:21.840 --> 00:31:26.920
Wow, look at that.

00:31:26.080 --> 00:31:27.720
Wow.

00:31:27.120 --> 00:31:31.120
She's really gone to town.

00:31:32.120 --> 00:31:35.800
Full marks for presentation.

00:31:36.960 --> 00:31:39.800
Looks like someone might have to eat their words.

00:31:43.640 --> 00:31:49.040
Mr and Mrs Haslam, Mr Carlsson.

00:31:49.400 --> 00:31:50.960
Er...

00:31:50.160 --> 00:31:53.160
We're early.

00:31:52.200 --> 00:31:53.720
We're ready!

00:31:52.840 --> 00:31:54.760
Please, sit down.

00:31:56.720 --> 00:31:58.360
Here we go.

00:31:57.600 --> 00:31:59.040
Thank you.

00:31:59.640 --> 00:32:04.000
Guys, I love you!

00:32:03.560 --> 00:32:06.080
You all know what you're doing.

00:32:05.200 --> 00:32:07.400
Hopefully.

00:32:06.760 --> 00:32:12.920
I don't need to say how critical it is that this goes off without a hitch.

00:32:12.040 --> 00:32:14.200
Kaz, you're absolutely sure?

00:32:13.440 --> 00:32:18.040
You say that again and I'll do you for discrimination!

00:32:17.080 --> 00:32:21.000
Fine!

00:32:20.440 --> 00:32:21.600
Let's do it, guys.

00:32:21.440 --> 00:32:23.520
And the game yesterday.

00:32:22.600 --> 00:32:26.640
You saw United at Liverpool?

00:32:25.720 --> 00:32:26.960
Mm.

00:32:26.040 --> 00:32:28.360
Game was fine.

00:32:27.680 --> 00:32:29.880
Could've done without the side-show though.

00:32:29.160 --> 00:32:33.400
We had this appalling yob behind us.

00:32:33.000 --> 00:32:36.040
One of the old '80s brigade.

00:32:35.840 --> 00:32:37.000
Archaic ideas, mouth like a sewer.

00:32:36.240 --> 00:32:39.400
Vinny soon sorted it.

00:32:39.120 --> 00:32:41.960
You had him ejected?

00:32:41.120 --> 00:32:42.520
Her.

00:32:41.720 --> 00:32:43.360
It was a woman.

00:32:53.800 --> 00:32:55.920
No offence.

00:32:55.000 --> 00:32:58.080
But I feel safer with you behind the scenes.

00:33:00.200 --> 00:33:01.680
Hiya.

00:33:01.040 --> 00:33:04.200
I'm trying to book a cab.

00:33:04.640 --> 00:33:06.480
This way, guys!

00:33:20.520 --> 00:33:24.560
Cheers.

00:33:31.880 --> 00:33:35.200
At least it's, er, decent wine.

00:33:49.880 --> 00:33:56.160
I'd like to tell you a bit about each dish before we serve.

00:33:55.280 --> 00:33:58.280
We're starting with a little amuse-bouche.

00:33:57.480 --> 00:34:08.360
Parmesan tuilles with a green pea and mint sorbet and a ginger and celeriac coulis.

00:34:09.800 --> 00:34:12.880
Ginger what?

00:34:16.120 --> 00:34:17.760
Thank you.

00:34:19.440 --> 00:34:22.639
Just look at the way this is arranged!

00:34:21.800 --> 00:34:24.800
Marvellous.

00:34:24.159 --> 00:34:27.840
Let's try it.

00:34:26.960 --> 00:34:29.400
Have you had this before?

00:34:30.400 --> 00:34:34.199
Doesn't it look delicious.

00:34:49.440 --> 00:34:53.080
So what do you do here?

00:34:52.120 --> 00:34:57.080
Well, I play old songs, look at old photos.

00:34:57.120 --> 00:35:01.400
Stick pins in effigies of Dan.

00:35:01.000 --> 00:35:03.840
It's an investment.

00:35:03.040 --> 00:35:07.920
It's an office cum kid-free Nita free zone.

00:35:07.120 --> 00:35:09.280
How often d'you use it?

00:35:09.000 --> 00:35:10.160
Less than you'd think.

00:35:09.240 --> 00:35:12.360
Actually I own the whole house.

00:35:11.560 --> 00:35:14.800
I own lots of houses.

00:35:14.040 --> 00:35:15.880
But Nita thinks...

00:35:15.000 --> 00:35:17.640
She think I'm just a carpenter.

00:35:16.760 --> 00:35:19.160
Which of course officially I am.

00:35:18.320 --> 00:35:21.680
But I've got a very healthy sideline.

00:35:20.960 --> 00:35:24.360
About which she knows nothing.

00:35:23.520 --> 00:35:24.720
Because if she did...

00:35:23.760 --> 00:35:25.880
She'd wanna get involved!

00:35:25.120 --> 00:35:30.600
And I don't much care for the way she does business, so I keep it under wraps.

00:35:29.720 --> 00:35:32.920
Wise man.

00:35:32.360 --> 00:35:34.960
And this is just small-talk.

00:35:35.200 --> 00:35:37.480
I know.

00:35:37.200 --> 00:35:40.240
That's OK.

00:35:39.280 --> 00:35:41.680
I've got all day.

00:35:42.160 --> 00:35:43.840
What about you?

00:35:47.840 --> 00:35:50.080
CROCKERY CLATTERS Oh, sorry about that.

00:35:49.160 --> 00:35:50.680
You still here?

00:35:50.960 --> 00:35:54.400
Don't I get time off for good behaviour?

00:35:53.600 --> 00:35:56.760
When I see some, I'll let you know!

00:35:56.040 --> 00:35:58.920
Look, I really need something in the next half hour.

00:36:00.720 --> 00:36:02.360
Ethan?

00:36:01.520 --> 00:36:03.000
All right?

00:36:04.880 --> 00:36:06.880
I'll pop this on there.

00:36:11.720 --> 00:36:15.440
Whoa!

00:36:14.560 --> 00:36:15.880
Hey!

00:36:15.000 --> 00:36:16.880
What the hell d'you think you're doing?!

00:36:16.360 --> 00:36:17.600
It's cool!

00:36:16.800 --> 00:36:19.400
We'll do this another time, yeah!

00:36:33.640 --> 00:36:35.720
I can't get a cab.

00:36:34.920 --> 00:36:36.680
No problem.

00:36:35.840 --> 00:36:38.400
I'll come and collect you.

00:36:48.560 --> 00:36:50.640
JJ, Georgie, Ethan, Arlo.

00:36:49.920 --> 00:36:52.480
Collect the plates.

00:36:51.680 --> 00:36:56.680
Remember, clearing from the right.

00:37:09.320 --> 00:37:10.440
Right.

00:37:09.680 --> 00:37:12.840
Ethan, move!

00:37:12.240 --> 00:37:13.520
Move!

00:37:12.560 --> 00:37:15.600
Two minutes, guys.

00:37:14.680 --> 00:37:16.640
Right, got it.

00:37:17.040 --> 00:37:18.400
Need some cutlery.

00:37:17.680 --> 00:37:19.880
What you doing?

00:37:18.920 --> 00:37:21.360
I'm seeing Bryce, OK?

00:37:20.600 --> 00:37:23.120
I've got an emergency session booked.

00:37:22.520 --> 00:37:24.400
Oh, please(!)

00:37:24.040 --> 00:37:26.040
I'll be half an hour.

00:37:25.640 --> 00:37:27.600
Are you off your head?

00:37:26.680 --> 00:37:30.240
Nita'll go baboon!

00:37:29.440 --> 00:37:32.080
Well, it's tough shit.

00:37:31.280 --> 00:37:32.360
Alice!

00:37:31.600 --> 00:37:35.480
I am sick of putting other people first.

00:37:34.680 --> 00:37:36.360
This is MY Sunday.

00:37:35.520 --> 00:37:37.840
It's MY appointment.

00:37:37.000 --> 00:37:38.680
Nita can swivel.

00:38:08.400 --> 00:38:15.600
Look, if it's a bad time we can easily postpone.

00:38:14.640 --> 00:38:16.560
No, no!

00:38:16.120 --> 00:38:19.160
I really feel like I'm getting somewhere.

00:38:19.000 --> 00:38:21.160
Like I'm on the verge of something.

00:38:20.560 --> 00:38:24.080
Another breakthrough?

00:38:23.320 --> 00:38:24.800
Yeah!

00:38:23.920 --> 00:38:25.880
Then we should definitely go for it.

00:38:28.360 --> 00:38:30.040
So.

00:38:29.280 --> 00:38:32.440
Are we ready to do some work?

00:38:31.480 --> 00:38:32.760
Deffo!

00:38:34.280 --> 00:38:36.960
Happy in your work, Dad?

00:38:36.680 --> 00:38:39.360
He doesn't get out much!

00:38:38.520 --> 00:38:41.360
I could be looking at a new career!

00:38:52.280 --> 00:38:56.720
Any plans for the summer?

00:38:55.960 --> 00:38:58.760
What is she wearing?

00:39:02.560 --> 00:39:05.360
She just doesn't get it right.

00:39:08.840 --> 00:39:22.200
For the second course, we have herbed filo purses filled with Brie and gravad lax, with a Meaux mustard and tarragon salsa.

00:39:37.040 --> 00:39:40.760
That's lovely, absolutely delicious.

00:39:41.000 --> 00:39:43.440
That's haute cuisine?

00:39:42.680 --> 00:39:46.320
Have you seen the flower?

00:39:45.400 --> 00:39:48.640
Looks like a small pasty.

00:39:48.000 --> 00:39:50.880
It's just beautiful.

00:39:49.920 --> 00:39:52.520
An edible work of art.

00:39:54.280 --> 00:39:58.720
Where's Alice?

00:39:58.000 --> 00:40:01.000
I thought I told you to stay in the kitchen.

00:40:00.040 --> 00:40:02.200
Where is she?

00:40:02.240 --> 00:40:03.440
Going deeper.

00:40:02.480 --> 00:40:08.760
Going deeper than you've ever gone before.

00:40:07.840 --> 00:40:18.480
All your limbs are becoming heavy, incredibly heavy, becoming so heavy you couldn't move even the slightest muscle.

00:40:17.840 --> 00:40:19.760
And yet, you're going deeper.

00:40:18.920 --> 00:40:29.000
And just when you think you can't go any deeper, you will step down to another level, another depth.

00:40:45.840 --> 00:40:55.000
And there, at that deepest level where you've never gone before, you'll find me waiting for you.

00:41:00.760 --> 00:41:11.200
WOMAN'S Help!

00:41:15.160 --> 00:41:19.840
So obviously there are things you wanna ask me.

00:41:19.240 --> 00:41:20.520
Such as?

00:41:19.560 --> 00:41:23.240
What I've been doing all these years?

00:41:22.280 --> 00:41:24.040
Not really.

00:41:23.400 --> 00:41:26.120
About Dan?

00:41:25.360 --> 00:41:26.760
Nope.

00:41:25.800 --> 00:41:28.320
Why I left?

00:41:27.480 --> 00:41:29.560
Seemed clear enough.

00:41:28.760 --> 00:41:32.760
You got a job offer.

00:41:31.920 --> 00:41:33.160
We'd hit a rocky patch.

00:41:32.240 --> 00:41:35.280
We might have come through it.

00:41:34.560 --> 00:41:37.280
You seemed to be in a hurry to leave.

00:41:36.560 --> 00:41:39.360
I assumed you had your reasons.

00:41:38.440 --> 00:41:40.480
Oh, I did have my reasons.

00:41:39.640 --> 00:41:42.600
You wanna give me a clue?

00:41:45.960 --> 00:41:50.160
Don't!

00:41:49.320 --> 00:41:50.960
Dad!

00:41:50.160 --> 00:41:51.360
Dad!

00:41:50.560 --> 00:41:51.760
Stop it!

00:41:51.560 --> 00:41:52.800
Stop it!

00:41:54.160 --> 00:41:57.000
What have you done?

00:41:56.400 --> 00:41:57.920
Dad?

00:42:08.480 --> 00:42:10.400
SHE SCREAMS Stop!

00:42:09.480 --> 00:42:11.600
Wait!

00:42:10.720 --> 00:42:12.840
Please!

00:42:11.960 --> 00:42:14.800
Let me explain!

00:42:13.840 --> 00:42:15.080
Can I?

00:42:14.200 --> 00:42:16.080
Will you let me?

00:42:15.200 --> 00:42:18.360
Bastard!

00:42:17.400 --> 00:42:18.640
No!

00:42:17.680 --> 00:42:18.920
Hear me out!

00:42:18.000 --> 00:42:21.200
I'm begging you, let's be calm about this.

00:42:20.400 --> 00:42:22.960
You bastard!

00:42:22.120 --> 00:42:23.480
OK.

00:42:22.600 --> 00:42:25.840
Number one.

00:42:25.000 --> 00:42:27.600
This was a major breakthrough.

00:42:26.840 --> 00:42:28.640
What?

00:42:27.920 --> 00:42:30.280
Warrior work!

00:42:29.440 --> 00:42:34.440
I mean I would never have dreamed of letting it go this far, only you asked me.

00:42:33.560 --> 00:42:35.080
What?

00:42:34.360 --> 00:42:36.080
You don't remember?

00:42:35.240 --> 00:42:36.920
That's interesting.

00:42:35.960 --> 00:42:37.760
What did I ask you?

00:42:36.880 --> 00:42:39.240
We went deep.

00:42:38.280 --> 00:42:45.960
While you were in the Regressed Hypnotic State, you told me that you had intimacy issues you were desperate to overcome.

00:42:45.160 --> 00:42:48.080
Oh, come on!

00:42:47.240 --> 00:42:50.160
You begged me to help you work through your inhibitions!

00:42:49.480 --> 00:42:51.400
What, by shagging me!

00:42:50.560 --> 00:42:53.360
Please don't use that word!

00:42:52.480 --> 00:42:57.280
I prefer to call it "Primary Intimate Congress".

00:42:56.480 --> 00:42:58.960
And it's what you wanted!

00:42:58.080 --> 00:43:00.880
I thought you were ready.

00:43:00.160 --> 00:43:04.440
If it's too soon, if you've lost faith in yourself, in the process.

00:43:03.480 --> 00:43:04.960
I haven't.

00:43:04.000 --> 00:43:05.880
Well, that's excellent.

00:43:05.000 --> 00:43:07.960
I have lost faith in you.

00:43:09.320 --> 00:43:12.080
Alice, wait!

00:43:11.240 --> 00:43:12.480
Alice!

00:43:11.560 --> 00:43:14.400
There's something you need to know.

00:43:13.520 --> 00:43:17.400
What you're experiencing is perfectly normal!

00:43:16.440 --> 00:43:18.640
What?

00:43:17.680 --> 00:43:20.240
Shock?

00:43:19.560 --> 00:43:20.720
Disgust?

00:43:19.840 --> 00:43:22.640
It's absolutely part of the process.

00:43:21.840 --> 00:43:23.680
And the next step.

00:43:22.800 --> 00:43:24.880
D'you want me to tell you?

00:43:24.000 --> 00:43:25.840
You're unbelievable!

00:43:25.040 --> 00:43:36.520
It'll come when you discover that beneath all this anger and outrage, and self-loathing even, is the realisation of what we've been working towards!

00:43:38.200 --> 00:43:40.680
That's right.

00:43:39.960 --> 00:43:42.200
Hey.

00:43:41.360 --> 00:43:46.640
See, somewhere in there you already know.

00:43:46.840 --> 00:43:49.800
Can you hear it?

00:43:48.880 --> 00:43:51.040
And what is it saying to you?

00:43:50.320 --> 00:43:53.080
Set me free.

00:43:52.440 --> 00:43:56.640
Let me tell you my name.

00:43:56.720 --> 00:43:59.240
It's desire, Alice.

00:44:04.880 --> 00:44:08.640
OK, so one day you're here, the next you're gone.

00:44:08.080 --> 00:44:11.600
No explanations, no calls.

00:44:10.800 --> 00:44:13.480
Maybe I thought you'd follow me.

00:44:12.720 --> 00:44:14.640
Maybe I thought I'd follow you.

00:44:13.720 --> 00:44:15.720
Why didn't you?

00:44:14.840 --> 00:44:17.240
Why didn't you invite me?

00:44:16.440 --> 00:44:18.440
Did you need inviting?

00:44:17.680 --> 00:44:19.280
Yes.

00:44:18.320 --> 00:44:20.520
Always?

00:44:34.240 --> 00:44:36.160
Oh, here we go.

00:44:35.360 --> 00:44:40.880
If I'd wanted to eat lettuce I'd move into a hutch!

00:44:40.040 --> 00:44:43.040
Is there any chance of a bacon bap?

00:44:42.120 --> 00:44:44.080
He's joking!

00:44:43.120 --> 00:44:46.240
Oh no, he's not!

00:44:45.400 --> 00:44:57.600
Arugula, pear and asiago salad with mango-infused olive oil and zucchini and red chilli garnish.

00:44:56.800 --> 00:44:58.760
I'd've been happy with scotch eggs and lemon meringue pie!

00:44:58.440 --> 00:45:01.960
You've no clue about haute cuisine!

00:45:01.120 --> 00:45:03.320
Nita, sweetheart, it's fabulous!

00:45:03.840 --> 00:45:07.040
Perhaps you should come and join us.

00:45:06.280 --> 00:45:10.240
Yeah, let the staff do their own bit for a change.

00:45:09.360 --> 00:45:12.720
Oh, I couldn't possibly.

00:45:12.040 --> 00:45:13.400
I like to oversee everything in person.

00:45:12.520 --> 00:45:14.480
Bad news.

00:45:13.600 --> 00:45:15.880
Sorry?

00:45:14.960 --> 00:45:20.000
If you can't trust your staff, why employ them?

00:45:19.120 --> 00:45:20.200
Well...

00:45:19.600 --> 00:45:22.320
Do you want to know the secret of my success?

00:45:21.360 --> 00:45:24.480
Ask Sven.

00:45:23.640 --> 00:45:27.480
What do I look for in all my associates?

00:45:26.600 --> 00:45:28.600
Can they delegate?

00:45:28.120 --> 00:45:34.960
Secure in the knowledge that they've made good choices, got the right people.

00:45:34.000 --> 00:45:40.640
That whatever happens out of sight, behind their back, everything'll turn out fine.

00:45:42.840 --> 00:45:46.320
Have you thought of me, over the years?

00:45:45.480 --> 00:45:47.960
Every single day.

00:45:47.000 --> 00:45:48.200
Next?

00:45:47.320 --> 00:45:49.000
I've thought of you.

00:45:48.400 --> 00:45:50.080
I'm flattered.

00:45:49.320 --> 00:45:50.480
Next?

00:45:49.600 --> 00:45:52.280
I hated you for not coming after me.

00:45:51.600 --> 00:45:53.800
I made myself not come.

00:45:52.840 --> 00:45:55.000
I made myself stay away.

00:45:54.120 --> 00:45:57.640
I married Nita to get at you.

00:45:56.840 --> 00:45:59.240
I know you did!

00:45:58.280 --> 00:46:00.160
What were we like?

00:45:59.200 --> 00:46:01.520
Crazy.

00:46:00.720 --> 00:46:01.880
Intense.

00:46:01.160 --> 00:46:03.840
Couldn't leave each other alone.

00:46:04.040 --> 00:46:05.200
Still can't.

00:46:04.240 --> 00:46:07.400
Phil, what do you want?

00:46:06.880 --> 00:46:11.800
You could've come to the church and left after the funeral.

00:46:11.000 --> 00:46:14.520
Why are you still here?

00:46:13.640 --> 00:46:17.960
To bury this once and for all.

00:46:20.680 --> 00:46:21.760
How?

00:46:22.480 --> 00:46:27.160
OK, what if, just say, we've built up this whole thing?

00:46:27.680 --> 00:46:33.760
Each other, our three years together, into this amazing myth?

00:46:33.720 --> 00:46:39.160
What if the reality was much less dramatic?

00:46:38.680 --> 00:46:40.120
Is much less?

00:46:39.440 --> 00:46:42.160
Isn't worth wrecking lives for?

00:46:42.320 --> 00:46:48.760
What if we went ahead and trashed our families, blew our lives apart.

00:46:47.880 --> 00:46:54.240
And six months down the line we realised there was nothing to it, and all we needed was to get each other out of our systems?

00:46:53.920 --> 00:46:56.160
How?

00:47:01.880 --> 00:47:04.360
Just once.

00:47:08.040 --> 00:47:10.960
And then... we put the relationship...

00:47:11.840 --> 00:47:14.520
To bed.

00:47:13.640 --> 00:47:15.120
And move on.

00:47:14.320 --> 00:47:17.040
OK.

00:47:19.520 --> 00:47:23.640
Just once, then...

00:47:27.560 --> 00:47:31.320
Just once.

00:47:37.640 --> 00:47:51.480
It's a pleasure to experience a more refined cuisine.

00:47:50.720 --> 00:47:53.800
At least some of us appreciate it.

00:47:53.160 --> 00:47:59.720
Personally, I think it raises us above the level of the brute beasts.

00:47:58.920 --> 00:48:01.080
What?

00:48:00.120 --> 00:48:03.640
The ability to digest rabbit food?

00:48:03.040 --> 00:48:09.040
Perhaps we should have given some to our little friend from yesterday!

00:48:09.920 --> 00:48:11.600
Ahem.

00:48:10.880 --> 00:48:13.280
You don't recognise me?

00:48:12.600 --> 00:48:14.200
Sorry?

00:48:14.600 --> 00:48:18.240
Or my husband?

00:48:20.000 --> 00:48:24.320
Should I?

00:48:23.600 --> 00:48:27.800
From the match yesterday?

00:48:26.840 --> 00:48:30.480
You treated us to an outburst of your filth!

00:48:29.640 --> 00:48:32.800
And she calls me a liability.

00:48:31.960 --> 00:48:33.800
Did I?

00:48:33.160 --> 00:48:35.000
You don't remember?

00:48:34.280 --> 00:48:35.640
Nothing personal.

00:48:34.760 --> 00:48:37.920
I do it all the time.

00:48:37.040 --> 00:48:39.160
Get carried away.

00:48:38.240 --> 00:48:39.520
That's bloody rich!

00:48:38.640 --> 00:48:42.440
My wife was appalled.

00:48:41.520 --> 00:48:43.840
She's never heard such language like it in her life.

00:48:43.000 --> 00:48:45.840
Doesn't go to many games?

00:48:44.960 --> 00:48:47.840
Beth.

00:48:46.880 --> 00:48:47.920
Comes with the territory, expect verbal!

00:48:47.080 --> 00:48:50.600
They're United, not PC City!

00:48:49.720 --> 00:48:52.040
Mr Haslam, I really had no idea.

00:48:51.360 --> 00:48:57.200
I have serious doubts about your judgment if this is the kind of person you employ.

00:48:56.240 --> 00:48:59.440
What does it matter what she does on her day off?

00:48:59.160 --> 00:49:00.440
Alice.

00:48:59.480 --> 00:49:02.040
She's allowed to sound off if she wants!

00:49:01.200 --> 00:49:02.400
Alice!

00:49:01.440 --> 00:49:04.080
She said it weren't personal.

00:49:03.400 --> 00:49:04.680
You know, it probably was.

00:49:03.840 --> 00:49:07.880
Were you the knob-head calling Fletcher a spas?

00:49:06.960 --> 00:49:08.920
You don't slag your own team.

00:49:07.960 --> 00:49:09.840
Alice, stop!

00:49:09.000 --> 00:49:12.440
Beth, just take the plates and go.

00:49:11.520 --> 00:49:15.040
I think Beth had every right.

00:49:14.240 --> 00:49:16.120
Hey, and take this tripe with you!

00:49:15.720 --> 00:49:17.040
Hey, that's way offside!

00:49:16.120 --> 00:49:18.160
There's a lot of effort gone into that food.

00:49:17.400 --> 00:49:18.760
Has it?!

00:49:17.960 --> 00:49:23.840
Well, I'll tell you what, Sonny Jim, here's what I think it's fit for!

00:49:23.240 --> 00:49:24.600
And you know what?

00:49:23.760 --> 00:49:25.080
Here's what I think you're fit for!

00:49:24.200 --> 00:49:25.800
You little...

00:49:30.280 --> 00:49:32.320
Hey, hey!

00:49:31.440 --> 00:49:33.400
Dennis?

00:49:32.520 --> 00:49:34.760
I can't talk now.

00:49:34.240 --> 00:49:39.520
Well, I think you'd better cos it's high time we sacked the bullshit!

00:49:39.280 --> 00:49:42.720
Where were you the night Dad died?

00:49:41.880 --> 00:49:43.240
What?

00:49:42.280 --> 00:49:45.120
How is this relevant?

00:49:44.360 --> 00:49:49.960
See, I think he'd be on the warpath if he knew what you'd been up to.

00:49:49.560 --> 00:49:51.320
Course, maybe he does know.

00:49:50.760 --> 00:49:52.920
Maybe he is on the warpath.

00:49:52.080 --> 00:49:57.440
I can't talk now, I'm really tied...

00:49:58.640 --> 00:50:01.440
Make it go!

00:50:00.640 --> 00:50:02.040
Get it away!

00:50:02.920 --> 00:50:04.800
Over there!

00:50:04.480 --> 00:50:06.000
What?

00:50:05.800 --> 00:50:06.960
There!

00:50:06.120 --> 00:50:08.280
Who was it?

00:50:07.320 --> 00:50:09.760
An intruder?

00:50:09.320 --> 00:50:11.320
We should call security.

00:50:10.440 --> 00:50:15.520
There's no point, it wasn't an intruder.

00:50:14.880 --> 00:50:17.200
Someone you recognise?

00:50:16.560 --> 00:50:18.920
Someone you know?

00:50:18.080 --> 00:50:20.680
Yes!

00:50:19.720 --> 00:50:22.800
My father.

00:50:26.280 --> 00:50:29.440
Your late father?

00:50:30.560 --> 00:50:37.320
Father died recently, very traumatic, they were close.

00:50:36.520 --> 00:50:42.880
Then can I suggest that she takes some time out and sorts herself out.

00:50:41.920 --> 00:50:46.680
Because at this moment she's clearly not up to it.

00:50:46.120 --> 00:50:47.680
Tanya?

00:50:47.320 --> 00:50:50.480
There's nothing clever about overdoing it.

00:50:49.760 --> 00:50:52.640
Vinny Haslam's first commandment - know your limitations.

00:50:52.320 --> 00:50:55.120
Anybody fancy a Chinky?

00:50:54.320 --> 00:50:55.880
Wing Yip do an Earlybird Special.

00:50:55.040 --> 00:50:57.280
My treat.

00:50:59.600 --> 00:51:05.640
Nita, I don't know what...

00:51:11.360 --> 00:51:12.840
I think you should just go.

00:51:34.680 --> 00:51:40.920
You watch.

00:51:41.040 --> 00:51:45.320
This'll all be my fault.

00:51:44.840 --> 00:51:47.200
He's probably right.

00:51:46.280 --> 00:51:51.160
I have been overdoing it.

00:51:50.480 --> 00:51:59.560
I tell you, guys, when you start hallucinating, you know you're in trouble!

00:51:59.800 --> 00:52:02.920
I'll be fine in the morning.

00:52:02.000 --> 00:52:03.400
I doubt it.

00:52:03.080 --> 00:52:05.680
Thanks for the support!

00:52:04.880 --> 00:52:08.000
I just don't think it's all gonna go away.

00:52:07.160 --> 00:52:08.280
Oh?

00:52:07.400 --> 00:52:09.440
And why's that?

00:52:08.800 --> 00:52:12.160
Cos I saw him too.

00:52:11.720 --> 00:52:13.360
Yeah, yeah.

00:52:12.400 --> 00:52:13.680
I did.

00:52:14.800 --> 00:52:23.280
I saw Dad.

00:52:38.440 --> 00:52:42.680
Dan?

00:52:46.840 --> 00:52:53.640
I need to tell you something.

00:53:03.000 --> 00:53:09.400
'Hello, you've reached Phil Tyler's phone.

00:53:08.760 --> 00:53:11.360
'Please leave your name and number after the beep.'

00:53:10.840 --> 00:53:12.000
BEEP!

00:53:11.160 --> 00:53:12.600
Phil?

00:53:11.640 --> 00:53:13.960
I've come to a decision about the house.

00:53:13.680 --> 00:53:15.720
Call me.

00:53:22.640 --> 00:53:25.760
Nita, it's Dennis.

00:53:43.000 --> 00:53:47.080
Is this a social call?

00:53:46.280 --> 00:53:47.840
Not really.

00:53:46.880 --> 00:53:49.040
Dennis and I have some business to discuss.

00:53:48.720 --> 00:53:50.240
Well, that's weird.

00:53:49.360 --> 00:53:52.480
Dennis asked me to come round at nine.

00:53:53.960 --> 00:53:56.960
Well, don't just stand there!

00:53:57.840 --> 00:54:00.480
Smile!

00:53:59.520 --> 00:54:01.840
We're on camera!

00:54:02.160 --> 00:54:06.600
Another Oscar-winning performance?

00:54:05.840 --> 00:54:08.080
Look, I can come back later.

00:54:07.120 --> 00:54:09.880
Oh, that'd be great actually.

00:54:09.280 --> 00:54:10.400
No need!

00:54:09.560 --> 00:54:12.760
What I have to say will interest you both.

00:54:26.240 --> 00:54:34.560
As you know, I've had several offers for the house.

00:54:33.720 --> 00:54:34.800
Yes.

00:54:34.000 --> 00:54:36.920
Including, of course, from both of you.

00:54:35.960 --> 00:54:38.320
What?

00:54:37.440 --> 00:54:38.960
You didn't!

00:54:38.600 --> 00:54:44.560
Which I've considered carefully, and finally come to a decision.

00:54:59.000 --> 00:55:01.840
I've sold it.

00:55:01.160 --> 00:55:02.520
To someone else.

00:55:01.760 --> 00:55:02.960
What?

00:55:02.840 --> 00:55:04.320
Yeah.

00:55:03.440 --> 00:55:05.720
Made me a cracking good offer.

00:55:05.800 --> 00:55:07.800
Well, you shouldn't sell yourself short, should you?

00:55:07.640 --> 00:55:09.400
How much?

00:55:08.560 --> 00:55:10.120
I'll better it.

00:55:09.160 --> 00:55:10.640
No, I will!

00:55:09.920 --> 00:55:11.760
Sorry.

00:55:10.960 --> 00:55:14.760
I move out next week.

00:55:14.120 --> 00:55:15.520
Dennis, you can't.

00:55:14.800 --> 00:55:18.160
It's a done deal, I'm afraid.

00:55:18.160 --> 00:55:20.720
And I think it's what Dad would've wanted.

00:55:20.120 --> 00:55:26.720
New owners, fresh start.

00:55:27.280 --> 00:55:31.120
They're gonna gut the place from top to bottom.

00:55:34.480 --> 00:55:36.040
Ooh!

00:55:38.480 --> 00:55:43.200
That'll be them now.

00:55:51.560 --> 00:55:57.640
No, but I think Nita might.

00:56:08.800 --> 00:56:14.840
What you said yesterday.

00:56:13.960 --> 00:56:15.440
Desire.

00:56:14.480 --> 00:56:17.080
'Are you feeling it?'

00:56:16.280 --> 00:56:17.960
I might be.

00:56:17.280 --> 00:56:19.280
'I didn't get you out of my system.'

00:56:18.520 --> 00:56:21.400
Quite the reverse.

00:56:20.640 --> 00:56:22.920
I don't want this to carry on.

00:56:22.240 --> 00:56:24.760
It doesn't have to, Dennis, it doesn't have to.

00:56:23.920 --> 00:56:26.280
I'm really really sorry.

00:56:25.600 --> 00:56:28.760
She deserves to hear it face to face.

00:56:27.840 --> 00:56:29.360
Where are you?

00:56:28.480 --> 00:56:31.800
I'm with Phil.

00:56:31.040 --> 00:56:34.080
Nita'll find out.

00:56:33.120 --> 00:56:35.360
He'll have to choose, he'll choose you.

00:56:34.680 --> 00:56:39.160
Family falls apart, Nita flips, business folds, we're on the streets.

00:56:38.400 --> 00:56:42.240
Nita's out of control, Nita's as fallible as the rest of the human race.

00:56:41.440 --> 00:56:43.520
I think you need help, Mum.

00:56:42.560 --> 00:56:43.960
When were you going to tell me?

00:56:43.120 --> 00:56:45.120
What?

00:56:44.240 --> 00:56:50.360
About Mum?
